    "description": {
      "value": "You raise a fiery shield around yourself, gaining resistance 10 to fire. If you take fire damage that would reduce you to 0 Hit Points, the phoenix ward absorbs any damage beyond the amount that would bring you to 1 Hit Point. The ward then heals you in a brilliant display of flames in the shape of a phoenix's wings and envelop you in light. You regain Hit Points equal to 4d8 + the absorbed damage; this is a healing vitality effect. The phoenix ward then ends, and you can't cast it again for 24 hours."
    },
    "higher_level_description": {
      "value": "Heightened (+1): The healing increases by 1d8."
    },
